      note: "miso-113 phase 2: INERT once actually WIRED (cell O -> I). THE MECHANISM NEVER FIRED IN THE MERGED STATE: it was threaded into pipeline/year.py and runner.py only, while scripts/run_calibration.py — the orchestrator every calibration arm and keeper actually runs — builds its OWN p1_fleet_prep= chain and never constructed the hook (run_calibration carried only the config kwarg). An armed run was accepted, recorded armed in run_config.json, solved to completion, and the floor never applied: no error, no log line, the nyiso-87 failure mode verbatim — which is why this lane had a registered control and no arm. tests/unit/pipeline/test_p1_prep_wiring.py exists to catch exactly this but its _BRIDGE_BUILDERS registry is hand-maintained and did not carry the builder; the row is now added and the guard verified to fail on the real bug. The fix is WIRING ONLY — construction, scope, level and window untouched. A/B at the fixed HEAD (2026-08-02-miso-113c-control / 2026-08-02-miso-113b-night-floor; a fresh control was needed because 2026-08-01-miso-113a-control was solved at 247e795 and scenarios.py/schedulable.py/arrays.py/runner.py all changed before 1d3ec21). Control reproduces the 109b keeper at L1 0.00000% (2023/24) with the pre-existing 0.03007% 2025 HEAD drift. THE MECHANISM FIRES: 197 scoped tranches, 116,616/115,320/123,912 unit-hours floored, 15.89/15.41/17.39 TWh of floor volume, 97/79/85 committed blocks NONE shorter than 24h and most >168h (the declared baseload committed-run window, no clock banding), D-2 id 22 present on 115,728 unit-hours. It is legitimate by every rule-17/20 test — forced share 1.3/2.5/0.5% of COAL energy vs a 30% budget, D-4 off-window binding 0.0% all years. AND IT CHANGES NOTHING SCORED: class-hour L1 vs its own control 0.020/0.018/0.023%, COAL_PRB energy delta 0.000 TWh every year, D-1 IDENTICAL to 3 dp (cv_ratio 0.466/0.475/0.314 in BOTH arms, profile_r 0.988/0.978/0.971), C-series identical criterion for criterion (C1 16/16 free 12/12, C2/C3b/C4/C8 PASS, C3a FAIL -14.2% 2025 in BOTH, C3c FAIL, C7 FAIL on the same three cells with the same numbers), and IDENTICAL TO FOUR DECIMALS on the per-plant night-level statistic it exists to move (_miso113_night_level_test.py: measured 0.4343; control 0.4957/0.4482/0.5666, arm 0.4957/0.4482/0.5666). WHY INERT — two compounding reasons, neither the miso-111 LSL argument: (1) the keeper ALREADY SITS ABOVE the measured night level (0.4957/0.4482/0.5666 vs 0.4343), so a floor there is slack in most hours by construction; (2) where it does bind the plant absorbs it INTERNALLY — the eligibility gate (_ra_bridge_unit_params rejects binned incremental tranches) floors only the _committed band, so _econ/_peak give back exactly what the floor forces and only the composition inside the plant moves. That same gate also clips the level: 18 of 26 regulated plants carry a floor above their _mustrun band (69.2% of regulated-PRB nameplate, 4,274 MW) but 911 MW of it, on 12 of those 18, sits ABOVE the plant's _committed capacity and is discarded — so on two thirds of the clearing plants the applied floor is BELOW the night_p50 the field docstring targets. DO NOT ITERATE THE SIZING. Widening the floor to the full measured level (fill-order spread committed -> econ) was built and tested independently in this session's phase 1 and is WORSE, not better: C7 cv_ratio 0.466->0.460 and 0.475->0.420 (worse than control in the two years that had to clear 0.5), C3a -14.2->-15.8%, C3b PASS->FAIL. The reason is structural, not a sizing question: C7's failure is that the model's overnight distribution is too NARROW and a LOWER BOUND CAN ONLY NARROW IT FURTHER — a slack floor changes nothing, a binding one clips the cheap hours that are the entire source of the model's off-peak variability. THIS CLOSES THE REGULATED-PRB SELF-COMMITMENT FAMILY in all three admissible forms: whole-band repricing (miso-111, R), per-plant split (miso-112, R), night-level floor (miso-113, I). Jointly they establish that COAL_PRB's C7 failure is NOT a coal-conduct defect — the class's night level, volume (C1 16/16) and phase (profile_r 0.97-0.99) are all right. What is missing is the DISPERSION OF THE OVERNIGHT PRICE SIGNAL (model off-peak p10 $29.71 vs actual hub p10 $17.95), the data-blocked miso-78/79 congestion + sub-hourly-RT lane, which now carries the C7 COAL_PRB residual in ALL THREE years. No successor is chartered; rule 19 forbids stacking a fourth coal mechanism on a price-formation residual.",
