      note: "ercot-173 (2026-08-06): the ercot-172-SPECIFIED correction of the open root cause recorded on the two event-cap cells directly above, BUILT under one gate, solved ONCE full-span, **REJECTED-AS-ARMED on three pre-registered non-renegotiable gates** (PRECOMMIT-ercot172 §5 inherited verbatim via PRECOMMIT-ercot173 §5; runs 2026-08-06-run173a-reconc-control + 2026-08-06-run173b-event-cap-reconc, both registered). C1 grain repair: partial_outage_derate_factors keys by the extract's own (oris_code, plant_group) in both ERCOT consumers — provably inert on the current bins sheet (SP-3), wiring correctness. C2 rule-19 reconciliation: the cap CEILING composes its armed measured layers by min() instead of the product (the ercot-172 double-count: W A Parish 0.6995 x 0.3630 = 0.2539 vs own-hour CEMS 0.7843). Zero fitted parameters; seam proof SP-1/2/3 EXACT pre-solve. **THE 2024 OBJECT BEHAVES EXACTLY AS ATTRIBUTED**: +1,118.8 MW restored at h2827 (>= shed 565.1, CLEARS), +353.3 MW at h3067 (< 550.3, shrinks) — both as pre-registered; shed 2->1 (G-SHED PASS), spike-day day-mean |err| 382->120 / 268->227 $/h, C3a-2024 +10.45%->+3.05% lw-hub, NRMSE-2024 3.00->2.26, spurious falls every year (G-SPUR PASS), G-DOF/G-D2 PASS. **BUT the blanket min() over-restores fleet-wide**: coal above the incumbent PRODUCT ceiling +0.98/+1.95/+2.73 TWh (bar +0.5 — **G-COAL148 FAIL**, the ERCOT-148/149 adjudication not survived), class annual energy far past the 0.5% band (2025 COAL_PRB +5.1%, CT_PEAKER -10.4%, ST_GAS -4.5%; **G-SPAN FAIL**), tail formation away from actual (2024 26->14 vs 53, 2025 3->0 vs 31; **G-C3c FAIL**). C3a-2023 (owner object) -28.48%->-29.71% lw-hub, inside the pre-registered band. STRUCTURAL READING (rule 1): min() is correct ONLY where the two layers measure the SAME units' downtime (the ercot-172 named plants); fleet-wide the layers are measurably DISJOINT at most overlaps, where the product is right. NAMED SUCCESSOR (own charter, rule 23): a UNIT-ATTRIBUTED partial extract so the cap min()s at shared-unit overlaps and multiplies at disjoint ones — also the discharge path for the ercot-167 SOC re-gate (RG-1 CLEARS on this arm). Keeper UNCHANGED at run168b; the incumbent product ceiling stays armed. *** ercot-174 RE-STAMP (2026-08-06): this row's R verdict STANDS, and the structural resolution it records is REFUTED at the grain it could not then measure. The named UNIT-ATTRIBUTED successor was built (ercot_dam_availability_event_cap_unit_scoped, row below), proven grain-only, and stopped pre-solve on its own AT-2 rule: the layers share units at 94-96% of both-active bin-hours, so rho = 0.9381/0.9585/0.9606 of THIS arm's ceiling lift survives unit scoping — the unit-scoped form IS this arm, not a refinement of it, and its G-COAL148/G-SPAN/G-C3c failures would reproduce at ~95% strength. The blanket min() therefore remains R, but for a SHARPER reason than 'the layers are mostly disjoint': they are mostly SHARED, the double-count is pervasive, and removing it collides irreconcilably with the ERCOT-148/149 product ceiling (owner adjudication, surfaced not decided). FINDING-ercot174-unit-attributed-partial-outage-2026-08-06.md.",
