      note: "REJECTED AS ARMED 2026-08-06 (nyiso-130) BY ITS OWN PRE-REGISTERED KILL GATE K6 — the IDENTIFICATION STANDS and is the durable result; the bare number swap does not. THE VERDICT: arming the published 940 MW collapses NYISO's modelled scarcity tail to 2 / 0 / 5 h against a measured 10 / 12 / 42 (control, which reproduces the keeper exactly: 22 / 3 / 24), so C3c fails ALL THREE years UNDER-produced with 2024 forming ZERO scarcity hours; and K6 FIRES because the downstate ST_GAS reliability floor takes up the slack, forcing +0.22 / +0.42 / +0.23 TWh more (share 20.4->22.2 / 22.0->26.0 / 15.4->17.0 %). C1/C2/C3a/C3b/C4/C6/C8 all PASS in BOTH arms and the pre-registered C3a adverse case did NOT materialise (mean LMP moves only 33.855->33.604 / 37.043->36.937 / 61.113->61.113). K1-K5 all PASS: exactly one differing scenario_config field, zero slack/dump either arm, in-window bound reads exactly 940.0 in the treatment and 325/275/275 in the control, no other link's bound moves, and the seam is EXONERATED (external import energy moves 0.000 / 0.000 / +0.047 %). THE STRUCTURAL READING, and why this is a rejection rather than a rule-1 [R-STRUCT] promotion: the arm does not REMOVE a proxy, it RELOCATES one. Zone-K reliability in this model is carried by TWO proxies — the too-tight transfer bound and the LI/NYC ST_GAS min_gen floor — and relieving the first loads the second, making the model MORE floor-driven, which is the opposite of what rule 20 [R-FORCED-BUDGET] asks of a structural change (floors are commitment scaffolding, not the dispatch model). It also leaves the model forming essentially no scarcity at all, a MECHANISM deficiency and not merely a fit one. The rejection is therefore NOT 'the residual did not move' (which rule 1 forbids as grounds): a protective gate fired, substantively. NAMED SUCCESSOR: a JOINT reconciliation of the transfer bound AND the downstate ST_GAS floor under rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH] — one Zone-K local-security representation replacing both — with its own charter and pre-registration. Do NOT re-test the bare number swap. Evidence: results/calibration/FINDING-nyiso130-li-transfer-security-limit-2026-08-06.md, PREREG-nyiso130-li-transfer-security-limit-2026-08-06.md, _nyiso130_ab_gates.json, _nyiso130_li_tsl_identification.json; arms 2026-08-06-nyiso-130-control / 2026-08-06-nyiso-130-n11-tsl, both registered. (IDENTIFICATION AS PRE-REGISTERED, UNCHANGED AND STILL CORRECT:) NYISO-EXCLUSIVE, and a RECONCILIATION of the already-armed nyiso_li_lcr_tsl (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]) — same link, same HB14-21 window, same symmetry, ZERO free parameters; only the published number changes, 325/275/275 -> 940 MW. THE DEFECT: the import_limit the cap reads is NOT the interface's transfer limit. NYISO's Locality Bulk Power Transmission Capability Report TABLE 1 note 2 says so verbatim and identically in the 2024-25, 2025-26 and 2026-27 editions — 'The true N-1-1 Transmission Security Limit is 940 in this scenario, the Bulk Transfer Limit accounts for the loss-of-source of 660 MW' (the Neptune HVDC) — and the published figure is the term the LCR TSL Floor Calculation consumes as UCAP requirement = load forecast - import_limit (2023 LCR Report: '[B] = Studied 325'), i.e. capacity-adequacy accounting, not a bound on an hour. WHY IT IS A DOUBLE COUNT IN THIS MODEL, which is what makes it rule-19 and not merely a boundary note: the 660 MW is already carried TWICE — Neptune's ENERGY on the separate NYISO_external->Long_Island link (measured seam envelope 1,012/986/990 MW, at bound 99.9/99.9/98.9 % of hours) and the RESERVE against losing it in the armed published Zone-K locational reserve ladder (nyiso_li_locational_reserve, cell K). BOUNDARY IS CLEAN: the TSL report's own Appendix A defines the Zone-K interface as Y49 + Y50 345 kV plus the two PAR-controlled 138 kV J->K ties with the UDR cables counted SEPARATELY — exactly the model's two-link split — and 940 MW is a NET Zone-K import limit (base case schedules 300 MW K->J on the PARs), so it maps onto this single net link directly. Every edition names the same limiting element at the same rating (Dunwoodie-Shore Road Y50 345 kV @ LTE 964 MVA), so 940 is ONE published constant across 2023-2025, not a per-year fit; the 2023/24 edition prints no true-N-1-1 figure and its row carries the 2024-25 value, the TIGHTER of the two candidates (implied 2023/24 ~ 985 MW). THE STAKES, MEASURED EX ANTE (probe scripts/probes/_nyiso130_li_tsl_identification.py): 100 % of the model's C3c tail hours in ALL THREE years are Long Island, inside HB14-21, with BOTH Zone-K import paths at their bound — so NYISO's entire modelled scarcity tail is formed at this bound, and the arm necessarily removes tail hours in the two years that do not want them removed (2024 already 3 h vs 12 h; 2025 24 h against a band whose lower edge is 21 h). That adverse case is PRE-REGISTERED as NOT a refutation under rule 1 [R-STRUCT]. ROW ADDED 2026-08-06 (nyiso-130) with the field, per rule 28(c); cell blank pending the pre-registered A/B.",
