      note: "NYISO REFUSED EX-ANTE, NO SOLVE, NO FLAG (nyiso-101), closing the follow-on nyiso-100 chartered. The limit IS real and published every capability year (data/raw/capacity-deliverability/nyiso/nyiso.csv, area 'G-J', import_limit 3,425/3,425/4,350/4,500 for 2022/23-2025/26) and the topology represents it NOWHERE — that premise SURVIVES; what fails is the boundary. THE HARD PART WAS NEVER THE EDIT. (1) MECHANICAL CUTSET TEST: the G-J locality is NYISO zones G+H+I+J and Capital_Hudson = F+G STRADDLES it, so no model link is a valid import-direction G-J edge — Upstate_West->Capital_Hudson and Capital_Hudson->Lower_Hudson each have one straddling end, Lower_Hudson->NYC is INTERIOR to G-J (capping it is category-wrong, not merely a rule-19 stack, and it is already the host of the NYC 2,875 MW cap), and NYC->Long_Island is a boundary edge only REVERSED and is already capped in-window by nyiso_li_lcr_tsl at LI's own published limit. (2) TWO OF FOUR REAL LEGS ARE NOT LP QUANTITIES: the F->G AC cutset is interior to Capital_Hudson (no column crosses it; Zone G carries 4,688/4,759/4,704 MW of Gold Book summer capability), and the external ties landing IN Zone G (PJM Ramapo ~1,000 MW + ISO-NE New Scotland/Pleasant Valley ~600 MW) are lumped into the 1,600 MW import_node->Capital_Hudson link whose F-vs-G split interchange/spec.py ITSELF calls 'a modelling choice inside the topology' — an undetermined allocation, not a measured one. Leg 2 is what closes the door: the endogenous workaround dissolves leg 1 but not leg 2. (3) NO VALIDATING SERIES EXISTS, IN PRINCIPLE: MIS P-32 posts seven internal transfer interfaces (CENTRAL EAST - VC, DYSINGER EAST, MOSES SOUTH, SPR/DUN-SOUTH, TOTAL EAST, UPNY CONED, WEST CENTRAL) and NONE is G-J, so the admissibility evidence its two accepted siblings have is unavailable. Run the house pattern's own test and the asymmetry is stark: the accepted NYC 2,875 MW cap sits essentially AT the p95 of its own interface's in-window flow (exceeded 1.8/5.0/6.9% of HB14-21 hours), whereas the G-J limit placed on UPNY CONED would sit at pctile 74.1/90.6/95.6 (exceeded 25.9/9.4/4.4%) and on TOTAL EAST at 67.9/81.5/83.4 (32.1/18.5/16.6%) — in 2023 forcing the model below measured flow in a quarter to a third of in-window hours. (4) A STATIC RECONCILED CAP IS UNIDENTIFIED, PROVEN NOT ASSERTED: translating via the Zone-G balance F_[F->G] + ext_G = load_G + F_[G->H] - gen_G needs (gen_G - load_G); load_G is measured (HUD VL in-window mean 1,168/1,207/1,231 MW) but gen_G is bounded only by [0, Zone-G capability], pinning the reconciled cap to an interval of width 4,688/4,759/4,704 MW = 137%/109%/105% OF THE LIMIT ITSELF. (5) PROVABLY INERT on the one uncontested representable edge with no solve: min(NYC->Long_Island 1,650, LI in-window cap 275/325, G-J 3,425/4,350/4,500) never selects G-J. HONESTY NOTE, recorded because it cuts against the refusal's rhetoric: the measured exceedance does NOT falsify the published limit — required gen_G at the in-window extremes (2,010/1,487/1,180 MW at p95, 3,545/2,605/2,994 MW at max) stays INSIDE Zone-G capability (76%/55%/64%), so the limit is CONSISTENT with measurement for an unobservable Zone-G net position. The verdict is UNIDENTIFIED, NOT REFUTED: the discrepancy and the missing term are the same size. DIRECTION PRE-REGISTERED AND REFUSED AGAINST ITS OWN INCENTIVE (rule 1 [R-STRUCT], both directions): a binding G-J limit tightens downstate supply and would RAISE downstate peak prices — the direction C3c, the sole NYISO determination blocker, wants — and that was pre-registered as grounds for EXTRA scrutiny, not encouragement. KEEPER UNCHANGED (2026-07-30-nyiso-100-silretire), no ScenarioConfig field added (so rule-28c CI has nothing to enforce), and the ISO's tightest cell (2023 CC_REGULAR, -2.80 of ±2.94) SPENT 0.00 TWh of its ~0.14 TWh budget. RE-OPEN CONDITION, satisfiable unlike C3c's: split Capital_Hudson into Zone F and Zone G, which makes leg 1 a real link and forces leg 2 to be allocated explicitly. The F/G county split is already carried per-county in zone_assignment.NYISO_CAPITAL_HUDSON_COUNTIES and Gold Book Table III-2a carries the zone letter per unit, so the fleet side is ready — but a zone split moves load shares, zonal shapes, reliability-floor limb keys (Capital_Hudson:ST_GAS), D-2 ids and every NYISO keeper's comparability, so it needs its own owner-authorized charter (the ERCOT West/Panhandle class, CLOSED). Do NOT re-test as a mechanism-flag lever.",
