      note: "CAISO KEEPER (caiso-138, owner promotion 2026-07-29; the caiso-134 §2 PNW firm-hydro dump observation). Reconciles caiso_firm_import_selfschedule with caiso_corridor_flow_limit (rule 19): the shaped floor is corridor-split DMM level x the TOTAL-system revealed shape, so on the near-balanced PNW corridor it exceeds the corridor's own p95 net-import envelope in a growing (month x hod) bucket set and forces 1.09/1.71/0.97 TWh out the WECC_PNW Dump at -$26.001 (node vs measured MALIN same-hours +$52.67/41.22/41.77). Clip = pointwise min of the two existing measured series, zero new DOF. A/B (prereg pushed pre-solve, all gates PASS): alpha-dump eliminated exactly to the beta bound (0.000/0.009/0.014 TWh residual = the SEPARATE negative-hub dump-gaming defect); CA-side LP byte-identical to control (E1/E2 = +0.0000, rubric unchanged NOT-YET {C3a-2025, C3c}); node reprices -26.00 -> +40.79/+37.46/+41.83 median vs measured MALIN +52.67/+41.22/+41.77. Also filed, NOT armed: the P1 sink-deletion seam (_bridge_floored_fleet max-composes a zeros floor over negative-pmin export sinks, deleting them in every scored P1 pass, all ISOs with sinks + an armed bridge — infrastructure lane; naive fix refused, U-turn gaps $1.28-8.54/MWh over 20-57% of hours) and the PNW firm energy-basis overreach (forced 9.2-13.4 TWh vs measured corridor net -0.5..+4.7 TWh — E1-adverse, upstream lane).",
